# Agent Workflow Boundaries

## Planned-Work Lifecycle

For **planned work** that changes code and produces SDDs:

1. **`code-investigator`** — when existing behaviour must be understood first (optional).
2. **`architect-planner`** — phased plan under `docs/sdd/<slug>.md` + ADRs; mark `DRAFT` until approved.
3. **Approve SDD** — requester clears `DRAFT`. Do not start phase execution while `DRAFT`.
4. **`phase-executor`** — one approved phase per pass on `<feature-slug>/phase-<n>`.
5. **`doc-sync`** — capture implementation Status / Notes (preserve `PR`).
6. **`test-runner`** — tests + `docs/sdd/test-reports/<slug>.md`.
7. **`doc-sync`** — verification status, coverage, residual risk.
8. **Parent agent** — when phase is **`Verified`**: one commit for that phase; open/update stacked PR **only if the user asked to push/PR**; then may start next phase.
9. **`rule-feedback-writer`** — after durable guidance feedback (typically end of feature).

## Standalone Subagent Use

| Subagent | Standalone when |
| --- | --- |
| `code-investigator` | Read-only how/where/flow questions |
| `architect-planner` | Vague or large scope needing a plan |
| `phase-executor`, `test-runner`, `doc-sync`, `rule-feedback-writer` | Planned work / mutations as above |

## Parallelisation

- Parallelise **read-only analysis** only.
- Never parallelise writes to product code, tests, config, reports, plans, or ADRs.

## Responsibility Boundaries

- `phase-executor` must not create/update planning docs, test reports, or ADRs; must not commit.
- `architect-planner` must not implement application code.
- `doc-sync` updates Status / Notes only; preserves `PR`; no product code.
- `test-runner` must not claim pass without command evidence.
- Parent owns commits; push only when the user explicitly asks.

## Guidance Placement

- `AGENTS.md` — broad defaults
- `.cursor/agents/*.mdc` — role workflow
- `.cursor/rules/agent/` — process rules
- `.cursor/rules/language/` — language practices
- `.cursor/rules/<framework>/` — stack rules
- `docs/adr/` — durable architecture
- Feature facts stay in SDD / test-report / investigation docs
